{
  "_source_key": "joback1987",
  "_description": "Joback & Reid group contributions, Table III (pp 235-238).",
  "_read_from": "a 300 dpi RENDER of joback1987.pdf pages 4-8, not the text layer",
  "_why_rendered": "The text layer substitutes PLAUSIBLE characters rather than producing garbage, so a junk-character metric scores those pages at 0.1% and calls them clean. Measured on p235: 5 of 119 values are corrupted -- '0.011]' for 0.0111, '0.0]68' for 0.0168, '0.00]9' for 0.0019 (digit 1 read as ']') and '0.0076' with a MIDDLE DOT for its decimal point. On p236 every ideal-gas heat-capacity exponent is wrong the same way: '1.95E + I' for 1.95E+1, 'l.53E - 4' for 1.53E-4, '-9.09E-l' for -9.09E-1. Every one of those FAILS to parse rather than parsing to a wrong number, which is what makes the cross-check below possible.",
  "_equations": {
    "_table": "Table II, p234, equations (2)-(12)",
    "Tb": "198.2 + sum(tb)",
    "Tf": "122.5 + sum(tf)",
    "Tc": "Tb * (0.584 + 0.965*sum(tc) - sum(tc)**2)**-1",
    "Pc": "(0.113 + 0.0032*n_atoms - sum(pc))**-2",
    "Vc": "17.5 + sum(vc)",
    "Hform": "68.29 + sum(hform)",
    "Gform": "53.88 + sum(gform)",
    "Cp": "sum(a) - 37.93 + (sum(b) + 0.210)*T + (sum(c) - 3.91e-4)*T**2 + (sum(d) + 2.06e-7)*T**3",
    "Hvap": "15.30 + sum(hvap)",
    "Hfus": "-0.88 + sum(hfus)",
    "eta_L": "MW * exp((sum(eta_a) - 597.82)/T + sum(eta_b) - 11.202)"
  },
  "_units": {
    "Tb": "K",
    "Tf": "K",
    "Tc": "K",
    "Pc": "bar",
    "Vc": "cm3/mol",
    "Hform": "kJ/mol",
    "Gform": "kJ/mol",
    "Cp": "J/mol/K",
    "Hvap": "kJ/mol",
    "Hfus": "kJ/mol",
    "eta_L": "N s/m2"
  },
  "_ranges": {
    "Cp": "273 to about 1000 K (paper, p238)",
    "eta_L": "from Tf to a reduced temperature of about 0.7 (paper, p238)"
  },
  "_notes": {
    "n_atoms": "Pc uses the TOTAL number of atoms, hydrogens included -- stated on p238, and easy to get wrong because every other equation is a bare group sum.",
    "printed_typo": "On p238 the nitrogen block prints '>H- (nonring)' where '>N- (nonring)' belongs. Recovered from the SAME table's other pages (pp 235, 236, 237), all of which print '>N-' in that position. Recorded rather than silently corrected.",
    "missing_values": "A dash in the paper means the group has no contribution for that property, NOT zero. Stored as null; a molecule needing a null contribution must be REFUSED rather than summed as 0.",
    "table_iii_is_rounded": "TABLE III AND TABLE IV DISAGREE, AND THE WORKED EXAMPLE USES TABLE IV. Table III (p237) prints the -Cl ideal-gas heat-capacity 'c' coefficient as 1.87E-4; Table IV (p239) prints 1.874x10-4 for the same group. Verified from the text layer -- '1.874' occurs on p239 and NOT on p237 -- and settled by arithmetic: 2(1.87e-4) + 4(-1.64e-6) + 2(-1.42e-4) = 8.344e-5, while 2(1.874e-4) + ... = 8.424e-5, and the paper prints sum(c) = 8.42e-5. So Table III is rounded to three significant figures and at least one group has a fourth digit the reference table does not show. THIS TABLE SHIPS TABLE III's VALUES, because Table III is the reference table and the fourth digit is known for exactly one group out of 41 -- adopting it would make one row more precise than the other forty for no principled reason. The cost is about 0.1-0.3% on Cp for chlorinated compounds, which the acceptance test expects rather than tolerates."
  },
